# A repo-local ignore file is load-bearing. Git's core.excludesFile is a global
# list, and on some machines it excludes *.sh and *.py -- so a new repository
# silently loses its own source. These negations re-include them.
!*.sh
!*.py

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# The advisory store. It is generated, it is ~34 MB, and it is per-machine.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Disposable output: build products, screenshots, working images, scratch
# notes. Nothing here is reviewed and nothing here is committed.
#
# It carries its own line because the machine this was written on hides it
# through a user-level excludes file, and a clone has none of that.
local.d/
